sieve-filter-v1
; English word order by part of speech (lenient): every word must be in the Moby Part-of-Speech
; list, its regular inflections or the names list, and each word must be able to follow the one
; before it. A word with several parts of speech may be any of them, except that a word Moby lists
; as a determiner, preposition, conjunction or pronoun is not also a noun, verb or adjective, and a
; determiner is not also an adverb (Moby gives "the" an adverb reading and "a" a noun one, which
; would let almost any order through).
;
; Which part of speech may follow which was chosen from real sentences, not by hand: starting with
; every pairing allowed, pairings were taken away one at a time while real sentences lost less
; than half what shuffled ones did, on three books of the NLTK Gutenberg corpus
; (Persuasion, The Man Who Was Thursday, Buster Bear), then measured on four others it never saw
; (Moby-Dick, Emma, Alice in Wonderland, The Parent's Assistant), sentences of 4 to 14 words that
; are all in the lists: 83.5% of real sentences pass, 42.8% of the same sentences shuffled, 41.4%
; of random strings of their words. That is a sieve for word salad, not a parser; moby-grammar-strict-v1
; is the stricter choice.
;
; The lists (beside this file; see moby-pos-v1.md): Moby Part-of-Speech II (Grady Ward; public
; domain), and the inflections and names tools/moby_pos.py makes from it and from SCOWL. Moby's
; codes: N noun, p plural, h noun phrase, V verb (participle), t transitive verb, i intransitive
; verb, A adjective, v adverb, C conjunction, P preposition, ! interjection, r pronoun,
; D definite article, I indefinite article, o nominative.
id        moby-grammar
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  English word order by part of speech (Moby), lenient: on unseen books 83.5% of real sentences pass and 42.8% of shuffled ones.

tokens    separator " "
edges     whole
set       det     tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:DI
set       noun    tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:Np-DIPCro
set       pron    tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:ro
set       verb    tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:Vti-DIPCro
set       adj     tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:A-DIPCro
set       adv     tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:v-DI
set       prep    tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:P
set       conj    tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:C
set       interj  tags:moby-pos-v1.tsv+moby-inflections-v1.tsv+moby-names-v1.tsv:!

follow    det     det
follow    det     noun
follow    det     pron
follow    det     verb
follow    det     adj
follow    det     prep
follow    det     interj
follow    noun    noun
follow    noun    pron
follow    noun    verb
follow    noun    adv
follow    noun    prep
follow    noun    conj
follow    noun    interj
follow    pron    det
follow    pron    verb
follow    pron    adv
follow    pron    prep
follow    pron    conj
follow    verb    det
follow    verb    noun
follow    verb    pron
follow    verb    verb
follow    verb    adj
follow    verb    adv
follow    verb    prep
follow    verb    conj
follow    adj     det
follow    adj     noun
follow    adj     pron
follow    adj     adj
follow    adj     adv
follow    adj     prep
follow    adj     conj
follow    adj     interj
follow    adv     det
follow    adv     verb
follow    adv     adj
follow    adv     adv
follow    adv     prep
follow    adv     conj
follow    prep    det
follow    prep    noun
follow    prep    pron
follow    prep    adj
follow    prep    adv
follow    prep    interj
follow    conj    det
follow    conj    noun
follow    conj    pron
follow    conj    verb
follow    conj    adj
follow    conj    adv
follow    conj    prep
follow    conj    conj
follow    conj    interj
follow    interj  det
follow    interj  verb
follow    interj  adv
follow    interj  conj
follow    interj  interj
first     det noun pron adv prep conj interj
last      noun pron verb adj adv
end
